{{!
    @template mod_starrating/mobile_course_page

    The stars as they appear inline on the course page in the Moodle app.

    The app renders this through core-format-text, so no app directive works
    here and the stars are plain markup. mobile/init.js gives them their
    behaviour: one tap saves the rating and repaints the stars in place, without
    opening the activity. Without that script they are a display only, which is
    also what people who may not rate get.

    The activity name has to be printed here: the app replaces the module title
    with this content, so nothing else would show what is being rated.

    The data attributes are the contract with mobile/init.js.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * name string Name of the activity, which is the criterion
    * cmid int Course module id
    * courseid int Course id
    * canrate bool Whether the user may rate
    * stars array List of value, on and label
    * statustext string The current user rating in words
    * showaverage bool Whether to show the average
    * averagetext string The average in words

    Example context (json):
    {
        "name": "Teaching quality",
        "cmid": 12,
        "courseid": 7,
        "canrate": true,
        "stars": [
            {"value": 1, "on": true, "label": "Rate Teaching quality with 1 of 5 stars"},
            {"value": 2, "on": true, "label": "Rate Teaching quality with 2 of 5 stars"},
            {"value": 3, "on": true, "label": "Rate Teaching quality with 3 of 5 stars"},
            {"value": 4, "on": false, "label": "Rate Teaching quality with 4 of 5 stars"},
            {"value": 5, "on": false, "label": "Rate Teaching quality with 5 of 5 stars"}
        ],
        "statustext": "Your rating for Teaching quality: 3 of 5 stars",
        "showaverage": true,
        "averagetext": "Average 3.8 of 5 from 12 ratings"
    }
}}
<div class="starrating-activity starrating-app-coursepage" data-cmid="{{cmid}}" data-courseid="{{courseid}}"
    data-canrate="{{#canrate}}1{{/canrate}}{{^canrate}}0{{/canrate}}">
    <span class="starrating-name">{{name}}</span>
    <span class="filter-rating" role="group" aria-label="{{name}}">
        <span class="sr-only visually-hidden" data-region="status">{{statustext}}</span>
        <span class="filter-rating-stars">
            {{#stars}}
                {{#canrate}}
                    <span class="filter-rating-star {{#on}}filter-rating-on{{/on}}{{^on}}filter-rating-off{{/on}}"
                        data-value="{{value}}" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="{{label}}">
                        <i class="fa {{#on}}fa-star{{/on}}{{^on}}fa-star-o{{/on}}" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </span>
                {{/canrate}}
                {{^canrate}}
                    <span class="filter-rating-star {{#on}}filter-rating-on{{/on}}{{^on}}filter-rating-off{{/on}}">
                        <i class="fa {{#on}}fa-star{{/on}}{{^on}}fa-star-o{{/on}}" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    </span>
                {{/canrate}}
            {{/stars}}
        </span>
        {{#showaverage}}
            <span class="filter-rating-average" data-region="average">{{averagetext}}</span>
        {{/showaverage}}
    </span>
</div>
